you know this peanut allergy
thing, is this new, like

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.640
because I read history a lot

00:08:16.599 --> 00:08:18.630
and never heard about it growing up at all

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.463
about peanut allergy.

00:08:19.463 --> 00:08:20.760
I said, Is this something
that developed later?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.593
And my father went,

00:08:21.593 --> 00:08:24.150
' Oh no, no. There was
always peanut allergies.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.500
Always. They always existed.'

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.646
Cause you know, this is a
scientist and he knows this stuff

00:08:28.646 --> 00:08:30.750
and, and I said, 'Really?
Well, what did people do then?'

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.134
He went, 'Oh, a lot of people died.'

00:08:33.134 --> 00:08:34.992
(all laugh)

00:08:34.992 --> 00:08:37.200
Just like there was a different time.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.033
There were other priorities.

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.480
Yeah yeah, there were other priorities.

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:40.710
Like, well we got nine kids.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.930
Well two of them just ate
some peanuts and died. Well,

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.010
Oh shit.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.450
the other ones seem to
not have the allergy.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.560
Let's keep moving.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.413
Let's get that burrow out
of the mud and get going.

